


# AGENTIC ST-T1024 — A12: INTENT ENVELOPE

**Status:** Draft
**Depends on:** A0–A10, A11
**Applies to:** User delegation to an agent

---

## A12.1 Purpose

A12 defines the **machine-readable, user-signed delegation** by which a user authorizes an agent to act on their behalf.

The envelope is the user's sovereignty made explicit and verifiable at the API boundary.

---

## A12.2 Structure

```json
{
  "goal": "buy <item class>",
  "constraints": {
    "max_price": 200.00,
    "currency": "USD",
    "merchant_allowlist": ["amazon.com", "walmart.com"],
    "deadline": "2026-10-01T00:00:00Z"
  },
  "envelope": {
    "spend_cap": 500.00,
    "action_classes_authorized": ["query", "add_to_cart", "checkout"],
    "action_classes_forbidden": ["change_payment_method", "change_shipping_address"]
  },
  "delegation": {
    "agent_id": "...",
    "expiry": "2026-10-01T00:00:00Z",
    "revocable": true
  },
  "revocation_endpoint": "https://...",
  "signature": "..."
}






12.3 Requirements

· The envelope MUST be signed by the user.
· The agent MUST hold a scoped, revocable token derived from the envelope. Never raw credentials.
· Every action MUST be traceable to an envelope clause.
· Revocation MUST be honored within a declared interval.

---

A12.4 Refusal Conditions

Any action not traceable to an envelope clause:

Any action in action_classes_forbidden:

Any action exceeding spend_cap:

---

A12.5 Relation to A11

The envelope is presented alongside the Agent Certificate. The certificate declares what the agent can do; the envelope declares what the user has authorized. Both must be satisfied for an action to commit.

---

A12.6 Residual

The envelope binds the agent, not the counterparty. A counterparty may still refuse an authorized action. The envelope establishes user intent; it does not establish counterparty consent. See A13.

